course: dictionary
lesson: 1200
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Bucket is a good example: a bucket is a container for carrying water, but it can also mean a lot, as in «it rained buckets». Read the words around it to find which meaning fits. Ask: does it make sense as a container here, or as a lot of something?
explain: «In spring toads walk back to the pond where they hatched; volunteers carry them across in buckets on mild wet nights.» Here bucket is the real container, because the toads are carried in it. Compare «Sparklers are put into a bucket of water when they finish.» It is a container again, and the words of water show what it holds.
explain: Some words are part of a fixed phrase, and the whole phrase has its own meaning. «A drop in the bucket» means a tiny part of what is needed, not a drop inside a bucket. «A bucket list» is a list of things you want to do one day. When you meet a phrase, think about what the group of words means together.
fact: A bucket is an open round container with a handle, used for carrying water, sand or other things.
fact: A bucket of something is as much as a bucket holds, so «a bucket of water» means one full bucket.
fact: In «it rained buckets», bucket is a verb meaning to rain very hard. This is UK slang.
fact: «Bucket and spade» means the things children take to the beach to dig and carry sand.
fact: A bucket list is a list of things a person wants to do one day.
exercise: «Volunteers carry the toads across the road in buckets.» What is a bucket here? | A tiny part of something | A very hard rain | *An open container with a handle for carrying things | A list of things to do one day
exercise: «It rained buckets all afternoon.» What does buckets mean? | A toad tunnel under the road | *A lot of rain | A few light drops | A bucket full of water
exercise: «My first try was just a drop in the bucket.» What does «a drop in the bucket» mean? | A wet day at the beach | A very large amount | *A tiny part of what is needed | A bucket with a hole in it
test: «The bucket of water was full to the top.» What does a bucket of water mean here? | A bucket with a little water in it | A pond with steep slippery walls | *As much water as one bucket holds | Water that has gone dirty
test: Mia's bucket list has skydiving on it. What is a bucket list? | A list of things to buy at the beach | A list of rainy days | A container for carrying sand | *A list of things a person wants to do one day
exam: «Water stays in a bucket swung fast over your head because the bucket's bottom keeps pushing it round the circle.» In this sentence, what is a bucket? | A list of things to do one day | *An open container with a handle that holds water | A tiny part of something | A very hard rain
